# folk-printer-watchdog configuration
# Installed as /etc/folk-printer-watchdog.conf
#
# Two kinds of lines:
#   KEY=value    optional settings (must be at the top, no spaces around =)
#   a table row  one per printer, whitespace separated
#
# Settings ------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCAN_INTERFACE=wlan0     # which interface to search (default: default route)
# MAX_SWEEP_HOSTS=1024     # don't ping-sweep a subnet larger than this
# PIN_HOSTS=yes            # keep NAME -> current IP in /etc/hosts (no mDNS here)
# FLUSH_STUCK_JOBS=no      # cancel queued jobs after the printer's IP moves
#
# Printer table -------------------------------------------------------------
# QUEUE     MAC                  PORT  NAME                 FALLBACK_IP
#
#   QUEUE        the CUPS queue name (see `lpstat -v`)
#   MAC          the printer's MAC address — the one thing DHCP can't change.
#                Find it while the printer is reachable:
#                  ping -c1 <printer-ip> && ip neigh show <printer-ip>
#                or from the printer's own network/config report page.
#                Use "-" if you don't have it (then only FALLBACK_IP is tried).
#   PORT         9100 raw/JetDirect (default), 631 IPP, 443 IPPS.
#                Decides the device-uri: socket://IP:9100 vs ipp://IP/ipp/print
#   NAME         optional hostname to pin in /etc/hosts, e.g. folk-printer.local
#                Use "-" to skip.
#   FALLBACK_IP  optional last-resort address to try before scanning. "-" to skip.
#
# Example — replace with the real queue name and MAC on folk-SVA:

folk-printer   3c:2a:f4:00:00:00   9100   folk-printer.local   -
